Package: lex1dx
Type: Package
Title: Fast 1-D k-Means with a 0.01% REE Tolerance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Sriram", "Natarajan", email = "nsram@users.noreply.github.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Partitions one-dimensional data into k contiguous clusters with a low
    within-cluster sum of squares. The default tuned pipeline sorts the data, collapses
    to M = max(4096, 32k) groups, runs a weighted wilber-interp dynamic program, and
    refines the cuts. Optional five-significant-digit grouping (mode 'sig5') is provided.
    The C++ core is shared with the Python and Scala implementations in the same
    repository. Objectives and defaults differ from 'lex1d', which remains the
    paper-faithful exact-quality reference.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: Rcpp
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
